((date 2026-10-24) (slug path-stability)
 (hypothesis
  "Path-stability chain (#3404; pre-registration a8ba322fc, rule = dev/plans/path-stability-fixes-2026-10-23.md at b5ce359b7): is the alphabetical tie order a fair yardstick for path noise, and does either stabiliser (SR = entry_fill_size_to_available at min fraction 0.5, SC = a smaller position cap) cut seeded spread without a do-no-harm cost? Arms A (Alphabetical, list perturbations p0-p5), S (Seeded tiebreak, seeds 0-5 paired with p0-p5), SR, SC; top-3000 PIT v12, 2019-2024. Rule: spread(S)/spread(A) >= 1.5 -> the alphabetical yardstick understates noise and chains measure noise with seeded perturbations; a stabiliser passes on ratio <= 0.85 (SR) / <= 0.6 (SC) with median within spread(S) of S.")
 (base_scenario
  "path-stability-2026-10-23: 24 cells (4 arms x 6), run tree 3db869d32, 2026-10-23 20:55 -> 10-24 19:49 PT; all 24 RESULT, 0 excluded, 0 void; V6 = 0 in all 24 reports and all 23 validator_diff -check V6 gates exit 0; deleted names p1 SHEN, p2 ODFL, p3 SLAB, p4 DECK, p5 DIOD")
 (window_id top3000-pitv12-2019-2024-path-stability-6x4)
 (baseline_label alphabetical-A)
 (variants
  (((label A-median) (config_hash alphabetical-p0-p5) (aggregate (((mean_sharpe 0.787) (mean_calmar 0.643) (mean_return_pct 165.5) (mean_max_drawdown_pct 27.44)))))
   ((label S-median) (config_hash seeded-s0-s5) (aggregate (((mean_sharpe 0.838) (mean_calmar 0.674) (mean_return_pct 180.5) (mean_max_drawdown_pct 23.29)))))
   ((label SR-median) (config_hash seeded-fill-resize-0.5) (aggregate (((mean_sharpe 0.797) (mean_calmar 0.634) (mean_return_pct 165.3) (mean_max_drawdown_pct 25.36)))))
   ((label SC-median) (config_hash seeded-small-cap) (aggregate (((mean_sharpe 0.600) (mean_calmar 0.521) (mean_return_pct 86.9) (mean_max_drawdown_pct 20.36)))))))
 (verdict Accept)
 (notes
  "ACCEPT as the MEASUREMENT DEFAULT for tie order (Seeded, tiebreak_seed 0), not a return claim. ln(1+R) SD across the six cells: A 0.0167 (range 0.046), S 0.2108 (range 0.530), SR 0.2088, SC 0.1205; spread(S)/spread(A) = 12.6 >= 1.5 (90 % F(5,5) interval 5.6-28; leave-one-out 9.2-39.3), so the alphabetical yardstick understates path noise. A-p0 (0.985) sits inside S's six draws (0.673-1.203): alphabetical order freezes one draw, it does not shift the level. Bias: A-tickers are 17.4 % of A-p0's 138 trades vs 10.0-14.3 % in the six S cells and 9.5 % of the 1999-2025 list union. WHY: max_buy_candidates = 20 binds in all 277 decision weeks and the cut lands inside tie groups (ADMA 2023-08-18 score-95 group, GLNG 2022-02-04); alphabetical settles every boundary the same way, a seed re-draws them, so each seed is a different draw of the same tail lottery. SR ratio 0.99 (does not stabilise); SC ratio 0.57 but median 0.406 below S (do-no-harm fails). User decision 2026-10-25: Seeded (seed 0) approved as the default, the rule's correctness exception (R3), #3404. CONSEQUENCES: chains measure noise with K >= 5 seeds paired by seed; the record is re-baselined as K seeds (#3404 verify item); G2b stays a default-off axis (REJECT-as-stabiliser, keep-as-axis). Writeup: dev/experiments/path-stability-2026-10-23/README.md."))
